WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.540
Hello, my name's Alex Bateman.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.460
Take your origami DNA template and turn it over so the white side is upwards

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.880
then fold the paper in half.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.560
Be careful to make the creases accurately...

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.880
...and to make the creases strong, use your
fingernails.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.940
Don't fold along this thick line, but turn the paper over,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.580
and we're going to fold along this thin line.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.500
Be careful to make the crease accurate, and using your fingernails make it firm.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.320
Then unfold the paper, and make the next
crease.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.850
Keep working away along.

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:05.830
Then, when you're about halfway along,
it's easier if you turn the paper round...

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.000
...and start again at the beginning.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.180
Now turn the paper over, and we're going
to fold the diagonal creases.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.700
Fold along the thin line.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.820
Carefully and accurately fold along the creased line

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:41.200
and make sure that the crease doesn't extend into the white border, and then unfold.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.020
Then move on to the second crease.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.720
Continue, until you get to about half
way along...

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.440
...and then you can turn the paper round and start at the begining again.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.400
Now we're going to fold the white edge
down.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.180
This reveals the letters of the DNA code.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.840
This is a long crease, so take your time
to make sure it's accurate.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:26.800
Turn the paper over and we're going to fold the white edge down again.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.560
Partly unfold the crease that you've just made...

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.280
...then turn the paper over...

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.720
...and repeat.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.040
The helix is already starting to form.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:59.320
Now turn your hands, and we're going to
twist the model,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.720
and push the two ends together.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.580
Be brave.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.060
Now we just have to do a little bit of
tidying up of some of the creases.

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:12.949
We'll move around the edge...

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.940
...gently making sure all the creases are nicely formed.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.760
Here's one that's not quite right.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.980
We'll just flatten that carefully...

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.420
...and continue on round the model.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.740
Now DNA is a double helix,

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:35.330
so when we finish this side, we have to
go back up the other side,

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.070
again gently flattening all the creases.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.620
You're almost done now,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.860
all that's left to do, is let go of the
model,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.280
and let your origami DNA form.

